#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

usage() {
    cat <<'HELP'
Usage: initiate [--ask] [--image TAG] [--archive committed|uncommitted|remote]
                [--keeper URL] [--bin DIR] [--no-tree]
       initiate --help

Make the Git repository in the working directory a garden, in the
ClankOS container. docs/initiate.txt gives the protocol.

At a terminal it asks what no option answers. Without one it takes
the defaults, and --ask makes it ask all the same, reading the answers
from standard input.

  --image TAG     the image the garden's commands run in: latest, the
                  default, or a version to pin, such as v0.0.1
  --archive KEPT  how the garden's archive is kept: uncommitted, the
                  default, on disk and ignored by Git; committed; or
                  remote, by a keeper
  --keeper URL    with --archive remote, the keeper's address
  --bin DIR       where the scripts go; bin unless given
  --no-tree       do not go on to responsibility-tree

Writes .clanka/config.yml, intray.org, lines in .gitignore, and the
scripts in bin/, as the image has them. Updates the managed archive
rules in Git's info/exclude from the saved configuration, including
child scopes. Keeps existing configuration and content, and commits
nothing. In an existing garden it also adds what is missing.

Exit: 0 done, 2 refused or usage; 125, 126 and 127 are clankos-run's.
HELP
}

case "${1:-}" in
    help|-h|--help) usage; exit 0 ;;
esac
exec "$(cd -- "$(dirname -- "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)/clankos-run" initiate "$@"
